cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If DistilRL supports your learning, teaching, or research, please cite the
  project using the metadata below.
title: "DistilRL: A Condensed Introduction to Reinforcement Learning"
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: Dong
    given-names: Youxiang
repository-code: "https://github.com/datawhalechina/distil-rl-introduction"
url: "https://datawhalechina.github.io/distil-rl-introduction/"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A visual, bilingual, 12-chapter learning path that condenses core ideas from
  Sutton and Barto's Reinforcement Learning: An Introduction and the University
  of Alberta reinforcement learning specialization, then connects those
  foundations to policy gradients, PPO, and GRPO.
keywords:
  - reinforcement learning
  - Sutton and Barto
  - policy gradient
  - PPO
  - GRPO
  - bilingual education
